    "created_at": "2018-04-27T20:09:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-27T20:09:58Z",
    "body": "If this is intended for use with existing APIs - particularly ones like localStorage which have been around for some time - there might be web compatibility concerns. I could imagine certain edge cases/misuses out there pushing names above 1000 characters.\r\n\r\nTo be on the safe side, it's probably best to investigate which limits browsers currently use for the relevant APIs - and potentially add a use counter to detect unusually long names as well.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
